<title>USA: Citizens Utilities executive resigns.</title>
<headline>Citizens Utilities executive resigns.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citizens Utilities Co said on Friday James Avery resigned as vice president, energy, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Citizens' president and chief operating officer, Daryl Ferguson, will continue to oversee the company's Vermont electric operations, the company said.</p>
<p>J. Michael Love, vice president, corporate planning, will oversee Citizens' Energy Sector pending the appointment of a successor to Avery, the company said.</p>
<p>The company would not elaborate on Avery's resignation.</p>
</text>
